  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/brevibora-dorsiocellata/",
      "html": "<p>The Eyespot Rasbora, Brevibora dorsiocellata, is a well known, classical aquarium fish. Sadly the species became almost forgotten in the 1980ies. It was Mr. Takashi Amano from Japan who was responsible for the comeback of the species. Amano often used a large school of B. dorsiocellata for his stylish tanks – a real eyecatcher!</p><p>The genus Brevibora has been separated in 2010 from Rasbora. Currently four species are known, but sadly in recent new descriptions serious mistakes have been made, so the names will change in near future again. For that reason we use the name that is best known in the hobby – Brevibora dorsiocellata.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/brevibora-dorsiocellata-emerald-eye-rasbora",
      "html": "<p>A small schooling nano fish that is perfect for those looking to add life and color into a blackwater biotope. Temperament: peaceful.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "beforeYouBuy",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/brevibora-dorsiocellata/",
      "html": "<p>For our customers: the fish have code 451802 on our stocklist. Please note that we exclusively supply the wholesale trade.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "beforeYouBuy",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/brevibora-dorsiocellata-emerald-eye-rasbora",
      "html": "<p>Be sure to have the habitat ready before purchase.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/brevibora-dorsiocellata-emerald-eye-rasbora",
      "html": "<p>Prefers soft, acidic water with low TDS, but can adapt to a wide range of conditions, including both fast-flowing and slow-flowing water.</p><p>Temperature: 72–78°F (about 22–26°C).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/brevibora-dorsiocellata-emerald-eye-rasbora",
      "html": "<p>Small foods such as pellets and flakes. Baby brine shrimp are perfect as live food.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/brevibora-dorsiocellata/",
      "html": "<p>Eyespot Rasboras are peaceful and undemanding fishes that can be kept even by beginners in the hobby. There is only one point that should be mentioned: the fish look best (most probably because they feel safe) when kept in larger schools, starting with 10 specimens – the more the better.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/brevibora-dorsiocellata-emerald-eye-rasbora",
      "html": "<p>One of its best traits is its natural schooling behavior, which can give character to a blackwater biotope.</p><p>Tankmates: they are aggressive eaters and can out-compete slower fish for food, so do not keep them with slow-moving and shy fish. Likewise, do not keep them with large fish that see them as food.</p>"
    }
  ],
